# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# `node_modules` is the entry that matters. The web image installs dependencies
# in its own `deps` stage and copies them forward; without this line the later
# `COPY . .` drags the *host's* tree in on top and wins — which on a Windows or
# macOS machine means native binaries built for the wrong platform, in an image
# that then fails at run time rather than at build time. CI checks out clean, so
# this is the difference between "works everywhere" and "works on CI".
#
# The rest is size and secrecy: a build context is uploaded to the daemon whole.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/

# Build output — regenerated inside the image, and stale copies confuse the
# trace that produces `.next/standalone`.
.next/
**/.next/
dist/
build/
coverage/

# The PocketBase binary and its scratch databases. The image downloads its own
# pinned copy; `.pb_data` is a local database that must never reach a registry.
pocketbase/.bin/
pocketbase/.pb_data/
pocketbase/.pb_e2e/

# Test artefacts.
playwright-report/
test-results/
blob-report/
.playwright/

# History and tooling. `.git` is the big one — nothing in either image reads it.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Never. `.env*` files are templates in this repo, but a build context is not
# the place to find out somebody filled one in locally.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Reference material, not shipped code (design-handoff/README.md explains why).
design-handoff/

# Docs and local notes. The image does not read them and they invalidate the
# cache on every edit.
docs/
*.md
!apps/web/README.md
